    "title": "Man arrested after 28-year-old man fatally shot near Oak Cliff shopping center - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Timia Cobb ,\n12 hours ago Erick Artea Lerma, 28, was shot and killed in the 4400 block of Dallas Fort Worth Service Turnpike in Dallas Tuesday, March 31, 2026. (Metro Video) A man has been arrested and is accused of fatally shooting a 28-year-old near an Oak Cliff shopping center Tuesday night.\nDallas police responded to the reported shooting at 7:30 p.m. in the 4400 block of Dallas Fort Worth Service Turnpike, police said in a news release.\nPolice have accused Anthony Rios Rivera, 32, of fatally shooting Erick Artea Lerma.\nRivera fled the scene before officers arrived, but he was later found and arrested, police said.\nRivera faces a murder charge and has been booked into the Dallas County jail.\nSign up for Dallas News newsletters here\nRead the original article on dallasnews.com\n2",
    "summary": "(Metro Video) A man has been arrested and is accused of fatally shooting a 28-year-old near an Oak Cliff shopping center Tuesday night. Police have accused Anthony Rios Rivera, 32, of fatally shooting Erick Artea Lerma. Rivera fled the scene before officers arrived, but he was later found and arrested, police said. Rivera faces a murder charge and has been booked into the Dallas County jail. Sign up for Dallas News newsletters here Read the original article on dallasnews.com",
